# nb_atob (2026-11-08): port of tests/nb_atob_test.sh (shell) to pal + case data (the owner allows no new .sh; AGENTS.md). Drives ONE page through nb_js_worker with the nb_probe op, no window. The probe is a DATA file (&.widgits/_shared-lib/harness/fixtures/nb_probes/atob.js); a new probe is a new .js plus its expected lines.
# ANCHORING: the console capture echoes the probe's own SOURCE, so every token is anchored to a line start with a leading newline (the echo begins with '>'); an unanchored token would match the echo and report a pass or a failure the run did not have.
# NEEDS the real worker binary (ops/+x/nb_js_worker.+x). That binary needs wasm3 to build, which is not in the repo (audit 2026-11-08 P1-5): on a stale binary this case FAILS loudly, which is the truth.
RESULTS | ../results/nb_atob.txt
ENV     | LC_ALL | C
CASE    | atob
SCRATCH |
COPY    | &.hq-apps/network/ops/+x/nb_probe.+x | np.+x
INCLUDE | ../fixtures/nb_page.pdl
COPY    | &.widgits/_shared-lib/harness/fixtures/nb_probes/atob.js | probe.js
RUN | $T/np.+x | --worker | $HOUSE/&.hq-apps/network/ops/+x/nb_js_worker.+x | --page | $T/page.js | --dom | $T/dom.txt | --href | https://example.invalid/ | --title | atob:fixture | --probe | $T/probe.js | --console | $T/console.txt | --load-timeout | 30 | --eval-timeout | 60
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | the-probe-completed-LOAD-and-EVAL
EXPECT_HAS | console.txt | \n=>ATOB_TESTDONE | the-probe-ran-to-its-end
EXPECT_HAS | console.txt | \nLOG\pATOB_TESTRESULT 6/6 | all-6-atob-assertions-held-binary-string-and-padded-tail
EXPECT_LACKS | console.txt | \nLOG\pATOB_TESTFAIL | no-assertion-named-a-failure
CLEAN   |
